;; A HIGH-LEVEL loop composed of sub-loops. This is the same behavior as the
;; flat `critic` manifest, but authored hierarchically: the top level describes
;; the overall loop, and the actual work and the finalization judge are nested
;; sub-workflows (mycelium.compose wraps a whole manifest as one cell).
;;
;; :start runs the WORKER sub-loop (manifests/worker.edn) to a terminal verdict;
;; a :done branch is handed to the CRITIC, which either ships it or sends it
;; back to the worker to keep going; :abandoned/:exhausted finish directly.
;; Select with config :run :loop "orchestrator".
;;
;; The critic's revise goes to :retry — the SAME worker sub-loop on a node of
;; its own — never back to :start: the beam driver's turn slice redirects any
;; edge returning to the entry node into :end, so a whole-run manifest that
;; routes revise to :start has each cycle run as a separate turn with a fresh
;; data map, and the critic's attempt counter resets every bounce (the same
;; data loss the feature loop hit live, run 3b8d2af5).
;;
;; This is the structural basis for multi-agent work: once a worker is a
;; composable sub-loop, a top level can run several of them — one per agent,
;; each its own loop — coordinating through the shared workspace and mailbox.
{:description "A hierarchical loop: a worker sub-loop composed with a finalization critic, authored as nested workflows. Same behavior as the flat critic loop, built from composable sub-loops — the pattern the feature loop generalizes."
 :subworkflows {:loop/worker "worker"}

 :input-schema
 ;; What a driver hands this manifest to start a run. mycelium checks it in
 ;; run-compiled BEFORE any cell runs, so a caller that builds the map wrongly
 ;; is told which key, instead of a nil surfacing several cells later.
 [:map [:branch :map] [:turn :int]]

 :cells {:start  :loop/worker
         :retry  :loop/worker
         :critic :gate/critic
         :finish :loop/finish}

 :edges {:start  {:done      :critic
                  :abandoned :finish
                  :exhausted :finish}
         :retry  {:done      :critic
                  :abandoned :finish
                  :exhausted :finish}
         :critic {:ship   :finish
                  :revise :retry}
         :finish :end}

 :dispatches {:start  [[:done      {:verdict :done}]
                       [:abandoned {:verdict :abandoned}]
                       [:exhausted {:verdict :exhausted}]]
              :retry  [[:done      {:verdict :done}]
                       [:abandoned {:verdict :abandoned}]
                       [:exhausted {:verdict :exhausted}]]
              :critic [[:ship   {:critic/decision :ship}]
                       [:revise {:critic/decision :revise}]]}}
